      "title": "SCSI: fix READ CAPACITY (10) LBA display to show raw zero-based LBA",
      "message": "SCSI: fix READ CAPACITY (10) LBA display to show raw zero-based LBA\n\nThis patch corrects the display of the Logical Block Address (LBA) in the READ CAPACITY (10) response.\nPreviously, Wireshark incorrectly added +1 to the returned LBA field and displayed that adjusted value directly as the LBA. This is misleading because the SCSI READ CAPACITY (10) command returns the last valid LBA, which is already zero-based. The +1 value is only meaningful for computing the total number of addressable blocks, not for labeling the LBA field itself.\nThis patch:\n\nDisplays the raw last_lba value exactly as received in the response.\nComputes total capacity using total_blocks = last_lba + 1 internally.\nLeaves the display of calculated total bytes/capacity unchanged.\nRemoves the misleading +1 from the LBA output.\n",
      "author_name": "lishiao144",
      "author_email": "1447175116@qq.com",
      "authored_date": "2025-07-18T23:13:36.000+02:00",
